      "title": "なぞの言葉は劇で語られない",
      "text": "The Sphinx's riddle is never quoted in Sophocles' Oedipus the King. Later writers give it: what has one voice, and becomes four-footed, two-footed, and three-footed? A human being. In these texts, there is no morning, noon, or evening.",
